{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"GROUND TRUTH gathered for stories A and C (answers the plan-review E4 blocks on 06ae): (1) Claude Code tool deferral is controlled ONLY by the env var ENABLE_TOOL_SEARCH (true|false|auto|auto:N), settable from .claude/settings.json's env block; it is ALL-OR-NOTHING - there is no per-MCP-server or per-tool non-deferral lever (docs: code.claude.com/docs/en/agent-sdk/tool-search). So story C's AC 'limit the always-loaded set to <=4 Serena navigation tools' is NOT implementable as specified. (2) AGENTS.md:173 'Serena's tools load at session start' is inaccurate as a claim about TOOL SCHEMAS: in this very session mcp__serena__find_symbol / find_referencing_symbols / get_symbols_overview were listed as DEFERRED, requiring a ToolSearch round-trip. The server connects at session start; its tool schemas do not load. (3) .claude/ is git-ignored (.gitignore:38) so any committed hook/settings must add a negation rule. (4) Project settings resolve to the MAIN checkout root, shared across worktrees - a hook landed here is not picked up by this worktree session, so story A must be verified by executing the hook script directly. (5) PreToolUse supports hookSpecificOutput.additionalContext; plain non-JSON stdout is NOT surfaced to the model, so the hook must emit JSON and must NOT set permissionDecision (keeping the normal permission flow = non-blocking)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785371968778325001,"uuid":"57008baa-f411-47c2-af38-8604c6818b96"}